    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tt030t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32,
   "y": 2280,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "research",
   "color": "mute",
   "nav": "research"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt031t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2280,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "Rhythm entrainment and sensory substitution",
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "tt032t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2320,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 77.9,
   "text": "Neuroscience research shows dopamine deficits in prefrontal-striatal circuits impair temporal pulse generation in the basal ganglia. But the human auditory cortex syncs naturally to motor rhythms. Moving time tracking from the visual field into background audio bypasses working memory load.",
   "size": "s"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt033b",
   "type": "box",
   "fill": "line",
   "round": 8,
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2420,
   "w": 341,
   "h": 125,
   "text": "“The brain does not count seconds in abstract numbers. It feels intervals through cadence and sensory shift.”<br><br><span class=\"c-mute sz-s\">Dr. Paul Bach-y-Rita · Sensory Substitution research</span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt034b",
   "type": "box",
   "fill": "line",
   "round": 8,
   "x": 627,
   "y": 2420,
   "w": 341,
   "h": 125,
   "text": "“I either spend forty minutes staring at the Pomodoro circle shrink, or I tune it out until it yells at me.”<br><br><span class=\"c-mute sz-s\">Ira · 21, design student with combined-type ADHD</span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt040t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32,
   "y": 2620,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "concept",
   "color": "mute",
   "nav": "concept"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt041t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2620,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "Kitchen cooking ritual",
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "tt042t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2660,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 57.9,
   "text": "Instead of treating study sessions like a clinical medical intervention, Tomatone frames focus as cooking a meal. Music lives in pantry jars, work intensity is heat, and sessions end by plating.",
   "size": "s"
  },
  {
